Write a Python module that translates a single patient-intake turn from
Spanish to English while preserving a pointer back to the exact original
wording, so every English field in the structured intake can later be traced
to the Spanish phrase that produced it.

Interface:

    translate_turn(text: str, source_lang: str = "es", target_lang: str = "en") -> Translation

    Translation is a dataclass with:
        source_text: str
        translated_text: str
        source_lang: str
        target_lang: str

Implementation: call an LLM via llm_client.complete(prompt: str) -> str with a
translation-only instruction — no summarization, no paraphrasing beyond what
natural translation requires, and no added information not present in
source_text.

Raise TranslationError if source_text is empty/whitespace-only, or if the
model returns an empty string.

This module is a building block for pipeline.py, which stitches per-turn
translations into the full structured intake with source_span citations (see
data/fixtures/sample_structured_intake.json for the target shape).
